      "writtenOn": "2017-05-09T19:20:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "handlePollStateResult() could be called for DATA_REGISTRATION_STATE alone if that comes first right?\n\nExample scenario:\n1) Device is on GSM family RAT (mRoamingIndicator will be -1) \n2) Device moved to CDMA RAT\n3) RIL reported CDMA DATA_REGISTRATION_STATE before the VOICE_REGISTRATION_STATE (its possible)\n\nhandlePollStateResult() will be called for DATA_REGISTRATION_STATE when mRoamingIndicator is -1. So i think the check is needed.\n\nNote:\n-1 is an invalid value which could be sent by RIL/modem if the tech is on GSM/UNKNOWN.",
      "parentUuid": "0c900f08_dae8724b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1672,
        "startChar": 49,
